value is [left_strings, right_strings]. Return unique strings from left that are absent in right, preserving first occurrence order in left.
Implement solve(value), taking one JSON array argument, without mutating that argument. Return only the complete replacement file in exactly one fenced python block.


Current solution.py:
```python
def solve(value):
    left, right = value
    return sorted(set(left) - set(right))
